-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part IV (pilot projects) and Part V (administrative provisions): THE SEAT LAYER, piece er5.
-- Text: the plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation of the Regulations, current to 2026-09-30; an unofficial reproduction,
-- not verified against the official text. This file is generated from a specification (it asks, and calls; it states no rule of its own).
--
-- SEAT: a person who has lost work, or cannot work because of sickness, pregnancy, caring for a child or a family member, or who is self-employed or a fisher,
-- asking whether they qualify for Employment Insurance benefits, how many hours or weeks they need, how much they would receive and for how long,
-- and what they must do or tell the Commission. Officials have no seat: the Commission appears only as the party whose duties and powers the person is owed or exposed to.
--
-- Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, a short text), one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- The records and the periods the layer-1 modules expect are built here, in each question's WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called.
-- Where a fact is the Commission's judgment (that good cause is shown; that a form is approved; that it is aware of a failure) it is asked as a yes/no fact about the Commission's side.
-- Where a fact is outside the range (a table of Schedule II.x, the periods of s 22(2) and 23(2) of the Act, the rate of weekly benefits) the person is asked for the figure the other provision gives.
-- A day the text refers to and never states (the day reg 77.1, 77.994 or 77.999 comes into force) is asked as a date.
--
-- Nearly every pilot project in Part IV has ended: the groups below say so in their headings, so that a form can ask "Did this happen to you?" before showing the group.
-- A question about a spent project answers correctly for the benefit period or the week it governed; asked about any other date it says the project does not apply.

§ `Employment Insurance Regulations, Parts IV and V -- the claimant's questions`

§§ `Reg 77 -- Pilot Project No. 1, periodic claims (ended in 1999)`
-- Only if this happened to you: you claimed benefits for pregnancy, for a new-born or adopted child, or to attend an apprenticeship course or program,
-- with a period of eligibility that began on or after June 30, 1996 and ended by June 26, 1999.

@export What is my period of eligibility for Pilot Project No. 1, if I claim benefits for pregnancy or for caring for a new-born or adopted child (reg 77(2), (3)(d)(i))?
GIVEN `my waiting period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your waiting period begin?
      `my waiting period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your waiting period end?
      `I claim benefits for pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim benefits because of pregnancy?
      `my pregnancy period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the period during which pregnancy benefits are payable (section 22(2) of the Act, with any extension) begin? (Any date if you do not claim them.)
      `my pregnancy period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that period end? (Any date if you do not claim pregnancy benefits.)
      `I claim benefits for a new-born or adopted child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim benefits for caring for a new-born child or a child placed with you for adoption?
      `my parental period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the period during which those benefits are payable (section 23(2) of the Act) begin? (Any date if you do not claim them.)
      `my parental period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that period end? (Any date if you do not claim them.)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of days`
DECIDE `What is my period of eligibility for Pilot Project No. 1 if I claim for pregnancy or for a child` IS
    `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(i)` waiting `I claim benefits for pregnancy` pregnancyPeriod `I claim benefits for a new-born or adopted child` parentalPeriod
    WHERE
        `waiting` MEANS
            (`Period of days` OF `my waiting period began on`, `my waiting period ended on`)
        `pregnancyPeriod` MEANS
            (`Period of days` OF `my pregnancy period began on`, `my pregnancy period ended on`)
        `parentalPeriod` MEANS
            (`Period of days` OF `my parental period began on`, `my parental period ended on`)

@export What is my period of eligibility for Pilot Project No. 1, if I claim benefits to attend an apprenticeship course or program (reg 77(2), (3)(d)(ii))?
GIVEN `my course began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the course or program you attend under section 25 of the Act begin?
      `my course ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end?
      `my course is an apprenticeship course or program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an apprenticeship course or an apprenticeship program?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of days`
DECIDE `What is my period of eligibility for Pilot Project No. 1 if I attend an apprenticeship course` IS
    `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(ii)` attendance `my course is an apprenticeship course or program`
    WHERE
        `attendance` MEANS
            (`Period of days` OF `my course began on`, `my course ended on`)

@export Am I eligible to take part in Pilot Project No. 1 (reg 77(3), (7))?
GIVEN `I live in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live in Canada?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking whether you are eligible? (Living in Canada is required only before April 1, 1997.)
      `I made an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an initial claim for benefits?
      `I made a claim to which section 26(2) of the Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, did you make a claim to which section 26(2) of the Act applies?
      `my period of eligibility began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your period of eligibility begin?
      `my period of eligibility ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your period of eligibility end?
      `I claim every week in my period of eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim benefits for every week of unemployment in your period of eligibility, each for pregnancy, for a new-born or adopted child, or to attend an apprenticeship course or program?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible to take part in Pilot Project No. 1` IS
    `reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` `I live in Canada` `the day I am asking about` `I made an initial claim for benefits` `I made a claim to which section 26(2) of the Act applies` period `I claim every week in my period of eligibility`
    WHERE
        `period` MEANS
            (`Period of days` OF `my period of eligibility began on`, `my period of eligibility ended on`)

@export Do I take part in Pilot Project No. 1 (reg 77(4))?
GIVEN `I am eligible to take part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you eligible to take part in Pilot Project No. 1?
      `I wish to take part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to take part?
      `I completed and signed the form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you complete and sign the form supplied by the Commission?
      `my form agrees there are no unmet conditions of entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the form record your agreement that, to the best of your knowledge when you signed, there are no conditions of entitlement that will not be fully met for each week after the waiting period (except earnings that may be deducted under section 19, 22 or 23 of the Act)?
      `my form agrees I will notify the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the form record your agreement to notify the Commission as soon as possible if you cease to meet a condition of entitlement that would reduce or eliminate your benefits for a week?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I take part in Pilot Project No. 1` IS
    `reg 77(4) the claimant participates in Pilot Project No. 1` `I am eligible to take part` `I wish to take part` (`reg 77(4) the claimant has signed the form with the agreements it requires` `I completed and signed the form` `my form agrees there are no unmet conditions of entitlement` `my form agrees I will notify the Commission`)

@export Must I tell the Commission, as soon as possible, if I stop meeting a condition of entitlement while I take part in Pilot Project No. 1 (reg 77(4)(b))?
GIVEN `I take part in Pilot Project No. 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you take part in Pilot Project No. 1?
      `I stopped meeting a condition of entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stop meeting a condition of entitlement to benefits at some time during your period of eligibility?
      `that reduces or eliminates my benefits for a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your failure to meet that condition reduce or eliminate your benefits for a week in your period of eligibility?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the Commission if I stop meeting a condition of entitlement in Pilot Project No. 1` IS
    `reg 77(4)(b) the claimant must notify the Commission of the condition as soon as possible` `I take part in Pilot Project No. 1` `I stopped meeting a condition of entitlement` `that reduces or eliminates my benefits for a week`

@export Am I treated as having made a claim for benefits for a week while I take part in Pilot Project No. 1 (reg 77(5))?
GIVEN `I take part in Pilot Project No. 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you take part in Pilot Project No. 1?
      `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the week begin?
      `the week is a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a week of unemployment for you?
      `my period of eligibility began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your period of eligibility begin?
      `my period of eligibility ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your period of eligibility end?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having claimed benefits for a week in Pilot Project No. 1` IS
    `reg 77(5) the claimant is deemed to have made a claim for benefits for the week` `I take part in Pilot Project No. 1` `the Sunday that begins the week` `the week is a week of unemployment` period
    WHERE
        `period` MEANS
            (`Period of days` OF `my period of eligibility began on`, `my period of eligibility ended on`)

@export Can the Commission end my part in Pilot Project No. 1, and as of what day (reg 77(6))?
GIVEN `the Commission became aware that I do not meet a condition of entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission become aware that you do not meet a condition of entitlement during your period of eligibility?
      `the Commission decided to end my part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission decide to end your part in the project?
      `the day the Commission became aware` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Commission become aware? (Any date if it did not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Can the Commission end my part in Pilot Project No. 1, and from what day` IS
    `reg 77(6) the day as of which the claimant's participation is terminated` `the Commission became aware that I do not meet a condition of entitlement` `the Commission decided to end my part` `the day the Commission became aware`


§§ `Reg 77.1 -- Pilot Project No. 5, choosing not to be paid`
-- Only if this happened to you: you were entitled to benefits for a week for which you received, or were entitled to receive, an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f).
-- The text never says on which days the regulation came into force or ceased to have effect; you are asked for them.

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 5 (reg 77.1(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period ended?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end? (Any date if it has not.)
      `regulation 77.1 came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 77.1 of the Regulations come into force?
      `regulation 77.1 ceased to have effect on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it cease to have effect?
      `I receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive, or were you entitled to receive, an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f) of the Regulations during your benefit period?
      `I am entitled to benefits for a week of that payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to benefits for one or more weeks for which you received or were entitled to receive that payment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 5` IS
    `reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` `my benefit period began on` (IF `my benefit period has ended` THEN JUST `my benefit period ended on` ELSE NOTHING) `regulation 77.1 came into force on` `regulation 77.1 ceased to have effect on` `I receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f)` `I am entitled to benefits for a week of that payment`

@export Does Pilot Project No. 5 apply to a given week (reg 77.1(6))?
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the week begin?
      `regulation 77.1 came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 77.1 of the Regulations come into force?
      `regulation 77.1 ceased to have effect on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it cease to have effect?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Pilot Project No. 5 apply to a week` IS
    `reg 77.1(6) Pilot Project No. 5 applies to the week` `the Sunday that begins the week` `regulation 77.1 came into force on` `regulation 77.1 ceased to have effect on`

@export Am I treated as having proved that I am not entitled to benefits for a week for which I chose not to be paid, under Pilot Project No. 5 (reg 77.1(3), (4)(a))?
GIVEN `I am included in Pilot Project No. 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in Pilot Project No. 5?
      `Pilot Project No. 5 applies to the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Pilot Project No. 5 apply to the week?
      `I chose not to be paid for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you choose not to be paid the benefits to which you are entitled for the week?
      `I made that choice after I was paid for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make that choice after you had been paid benefits for the week?
      `the Commission told me about Pilot Project No. 5 before I was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission inform you about Pilot Project No. 5 before you were paid benefits?
      `I took back my choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you rescinded (taken back) your choice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having proved I am not entitled to benefits for a week I chose not to be paid` IS
    `reg 77.1(3) the claimant is deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for the week` `I am included in Pilot Project No. 5` `Pilot Project No. 5 applies to the week` `I chose not to be paid for the week` `I made that choice after I was paid for the week` `the Commission told me about Pilot Project No. 5 before I was paid` `I took back my choice`

@export Must I repay the benefits I was paid for a week for which I then chose not to be paid, under Pilot Project No. 5 (reg 77.1(4)(b))?
GIVEN `I am included in Pilot Project No. 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in Pilot Project No. 5?
      `I chose not to be paid after I was paid for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you choose not to be paid after you had already been paid benefits for the week?
      `the Commission told me about Pilot Project No. 5 before I was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission inform you about Pilot Project No. 5 before you were paid benefits?
      `I took back my choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you rescinded (taken back) your choice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I repay benefits I was paid for a week I chose not to be paid for` IS
    `reg 77.1(4)(b) the claimant must repay the benefits paid for the week` `I am included in Pilot Project No. 5` `I chose not to be paid after I was paid for the week` `the Commission told me about Pilot Project No. 5 before I was paid` `I took back my choice`

@export Am I to be paid the benefits to which I am entitled if I take back (rescind) my choice not to be paid, under Pilot Project No. 5 (reg 77.1(5))?
GIVEN `I made a choice not to be paid under Pilot Project No. 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you choose not to be paid benefits to which you are entitled under Pilot Project No. 5?
      `I take back that choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rescind (take back) that choice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I to be paid my benefits if I take back my choice under Pilot Project No. 5` IS
    `reg 77.1(5) the claimant is to be paid the benefits to which they are entitled` `I made a choice not to be paid under Pilot Project No. 5` `I take back that choice`


§§ `Reg 77.2 -- Pilot Project No. 6, increased weeks of benefits (ended in 2006)`
-- Only if this happened to you: your benefit period was established between June 6, 2004 and June 4, 2006 and you were ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.1.

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 6 (reg 77.2(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `I was then ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When your benefit period was established, were you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 6` IS
    `reg 77.2(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 6` `my benefit period was established on` `I was then ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.1`

@export How many weeks of benefits may I be paid in my benefit period under Pilot Project No. 6 (reg 77.2(3))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `I was then ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When your benefit period was established, were you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.1?
      `the weeks the table in Schedule II.2 gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks does the table in Schedule II.2 give for your regional rate of unemployment and the hours of insurable employment in your qualifying period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid under Pilot Project No. 6` IS
    `reg 77.2(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` (`reg 77.2(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 6` `my benefit period was established on` `I was then ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.1`) `the weeks the table in Schedule II.2 gives me`


§§ `Regs 77.7 and 77.93 -- Pilot Projects No. 11 and No. 16, a rate based on the 14 highest weeks (ended in 2011 and 2013)`
-- Only if this happened to you: your benefit period was established between October 26, 2008 and June 25, 2011 (No. 11), or between June 26, 2011 and April 6, 2013 (No. 16), in a region of Schedule II.8 or II.91.

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 11 (reg 77.7(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.8?
      `the Fishing Regulations apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations apply to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 11` IS
    `reg 77.7(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 11` `my benefit period was established on` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.8` `the Fishing Regulations apply to me`

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 16 (reg 77.93(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.91` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.91?
      `Part VII.1 of the Act applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part VII.1 of the Act (benefits for self-employed persons) apply to you?
      `the Fishing Regulations apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations apply to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 16` IS
    `reg 77.93(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 16` `my benefit period was established on` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.91` `Part VII.1 of the Act applies to me` `the Fishing Regulations apply to me`

@export Do subsections 14(2), (4) and (4.1) of the Act and section 24.2 of the Regulations stop applying to me, under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16 (regs 77.7(3)(a), (d), 77.93(3)(a), (d))?
GIVEN `I am included in Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in Pilot Project No. 11 or Pilot Project No. 16?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the usual rate rules stop applying to me under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` IS
    `reg 77.7(3)(a), (d) and reg 77.93(3)(a), (d) subsections 14(2), (4) and (4.1) of the Act and section 24.2 of the Regulations do not apply` `I am included in Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16`

@export Which period is used to work out my rate of weekly benefits, under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16 (regs 77.7(3)(b), (c), 77.93(3)(b), (c))?
GIVEN `I am included in Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in Pilot Project No. 11 or Pilot Project No. 16?
      `my rate calculation period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your rate calculation period begin?
      `my rate calculation period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end?
      `my qualifying period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your qualifying period begin?
      `my qualifying period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end?
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `Which period is used to work out my rate under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` IS
    `reg 77.7(3)(b), (c) and reg 77.93(3)(b), (c) the period that the reference to the rate calculation period reads as` `I am included in Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` calculation qualifying
    WHERE
        `calculation` MEANS
            (`Period of days` OF `my rate calculation period began on`, `my rate calculation period ended on`)
        `qualifying` MEANS
            (`Period of days` OF `my qualifying period began on`, `my qualifying period ended on`)

@export What are my weekly insurable earnings under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16, worked out on my 14 highest weeks (regs 77.7(3)(e), (f), 77.93(3)(e), (f))?
GIVEN `the insurable earnings of each week of my qualifying period` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What were your insurable earnings for each week of your qualifying period, in dollars, leaving out anything paid or payable under section 24.1 of the Regulations?
      `my earnings paid or payable under section 24.1` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was paid or payable to you in your qualifying period under section 24.1 of the Regulations, in dollars? (0 if nothing)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my weekly insurable earnings under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` IS
    `reg 77.7(3)(e), (f) and reg 77.93(3)(e), (f) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` `the insurable earnings of each week of my qualifying period` `my earnings paid or payable under section 24.1`

@export How much of the insurable earnings reported for a pay period is counted for one week, under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16 (regs 77.7(4), 77.93(4))?
GIVEN `the earnings reported for the pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much insurable earnings were reported on your record of employment for the pay period, in dollars?
      `the days in the pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days are in the pay period?
      `the days of the week in the pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of the week you are asking about fall in the pay period?
      `evidence of a week's actual earnings is provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you or your employer provided evidence of the amount actually earned in a week within the pay period?
      `the amounts actually earned in those weeks` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What were the amounts actually earned in the weeks for which evidence is provided, in dollars? (An empty list if there is none)
      `the days of those weeks in the pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of those weeks fall in the pay period? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my earnings for a pay period is counted for one week under Pilot Project No. 11 or No. 16` IS
    `reg 77.7(4) and reg 77.93(4) the insurable earnings allocated to a week with no evidence of its own` `the earnings reported for the pay period` `the days in the pay period` `the days of the week in the pay period` `evidence of a week's actual earnings is provided` `the amounts actually earned in those weeks` `the days of those weeks in the pay period`


§§ `Regs 77.8 and 77.94 -- Pilot Projects No. 12 and No. 17, higher allowable earnings (ended in 2011 and 2012)`
-- Only if this happened to you: your benefit period was established or ended between December 7, 2008 and August 6, 2011 (No. 12), or between August 7, 2011 and August 4, 2012 (No. 17), and you were ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I.

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 12 (reg 77.8(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `my benefit period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period ended?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end? (Any date if it has not.)
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 12` IS
    `reg 77.8(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 12` `my benefit period was established on` (IF `my benefit period has ended` THEN JUST `my benefit period ended on` ELSE NOTHING) `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I`

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 17 (reg 77.94(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `my benefit period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period ended?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end? (Any date if it has not.)
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 17` IS
    `reg 77.94(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 17` `my benefit period was established on` (IF `my benefit period has ended` THEN JUST `my benefit period ended on` ELSE NOTHING) `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I`

@export What is the most I may earn from employment in a week while I receive benefits, under Pilot Project No. 12 (reg 77.8(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `my benefit period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period ended?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end? (Any date if it has not.)
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I?
      `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the week begin?
      `my rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your rate of weekly benefits, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I may earn in a week under Pilot Project No. 12` IS
    `reg 77.8(3) the maximum allowable earnings for the week under Pilot Project No. 12` included `the Sunday that begins the week` `my rate of weekly benefits`
    WHERE
        `included` MEANS
            `reg 77.8(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 12` `my benefit period was established on` (IF `my benefit period has ended` THEN JUST `my benefit period ended on` ELSE NOTHING) `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I`

@export What is the most I may earn from employment in a week while I receive benefits, under Pilot Project No. 17 (reg 77.94(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `my benefit period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period ended?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end? (Any date if it has not.)
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I?
      `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the week begin?
      `my rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your rate of weekly benefits, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I may earn in a week under Pilot Project No. 17` IS
    `reg 77.94(3) the maximum allowable earnings for the week under Pilot Project No. 17` included `the Sunday that begins the week` `my rate of weekly benefits`
    WHERE
        `included` MEANS
            `reg 77.94(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 17` `my benefit period was established on` (IF `my benefit period has ended` THEN JUST `my benefit period ended on` ELSE NOTHING) `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I`


§§ `Reg 77.91 -- Pilot Project No. 14, extended benefit period and training incentive (ended in 2010)`
-- Only if this happened to you: your benefit period was established between January 25, 2009 and May 29, 2010 and you were referred to a full-time course or program of at least 20 weeks.

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 14 (reg 77.91(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your benefit period begin?
      `the years I contributed at least 30 percent of the maximum premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 10 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium?
      `the weeks of regular benefits I was paid in the last 260 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of regular benefits were you paid in the 260 weeks before your benefit period began?
      `I had an active return to work action plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an active return to work action plan?
      `my return to work action plan became active on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it become active? (Any date if you had none.)
      `I was referred to a course or program under paragraph 25(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you referred by the Commission, or an authority it designates, under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act to a course or program of instruction or training?
      `my course or program is full-time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the course or program full-time?
      `my course or program lasts this many weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks does it last?
      `my course or program began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does it begin?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 14` IS
    `reg 77.91(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14` `my benefit period was established on` (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` `my benefit period began on` `the years I contributed at least 30 percent of the maximum premium` `the weeks of regular benefits I was paid in the last 260 weeks` (IF `I had an active return to work action plan` THEN JUST `my return to work action plan became active on` ELSE NOTHING) `I was referred to a course or program under paragraph 25(1)(a)` `my course or program is full-time` `my course or program lasts this many weeks` `my course or program began on`)

@export How many weeks of job-search period do I get under Pilot Project No. 14 (reg 77.91(6))?
GIVEN `the weeks of training I completed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of the course or program have you completed?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How long is my job-search period under Pilot Project No. 14` IS
    `reg 77.91(6) the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` `the weeks of training I completed`

@export On what day does my job-search period begin under Pilot Project No. 14 (reg 77.91(6))?
GIVEN `the last day I attended the course or program` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you last attend the course or program?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does my job-search period under Pilot Project No. 14 begin` IS
    `reg 77.91(6) the Sunday on which the period granted for job-search purposes begins` `the last day I attended the course or program`

@export By how many weeks is my benefit period extended under Pilot Project No. 14 (reg 77.91(4))?
GIVEN `I am included in Pilot Project No. 14` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in Pilot Project No. 14?
      `my course or program lasts, with any interruptions, this many weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks does the course or program last, counting any periods of interruption?
      `the weeks of training I completed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of the course or program have you completed?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how many weeks is my benefit period extended under Pilot Project No. 14` IS
    `reg 77.91(4) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` `I am included in Pilot Project No. 14` `my course or program lasts, with any interruptions, this many weeks` (`reg 77.91(6) the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` `the weeks of training I completed`)

@export How many weeks of benefits may I be paid under Pilot Project No. 14 (reg 77.91(5))?
GIVEN `I am included in Pilot Project No. 14` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in Pilot Project No. 14?
      `the maximum weeks the Act gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks does subsection 12(2), (3) or (6) of the Act give you as the maximum?
      `the extra weeks I attend the course or search for a job` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in the extended benefit period do you attend the course or program, or search for a job in the period granted, and have no benefits payable under subsection 12(1) of the Act?
      `subsection 77.91(5) has stopped applying to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the extra-weeks rule stopped applying to you (because a ground to end your referral exists)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid under Pilot Project No. 14` IS
    `reg 77.91(5) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` `I am included in Pilot Project No. 14` `the maximum weeks the Act gives me` `the extra weeks I attend the course or search for a job` `subsection 77.91(5) has stopped applying to me`

@export On what day does the extra-weeks rule of Pilot Project No. 14 stop applying to me (reg 77.91(7))?
GIVEN `a ground to end my referral exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any of the conditions under which the Commission may end your referral under paragraph 27(1.1)(b) of the Act exist?
      `the last day I attended the course or program` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you last attend the course or program?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `When does the extra-weeks rule of Pilot Project No. 14 stop applying to me` IS
    `reg 77.91(7) the Sunday on which subsection 77.91(5) ceases to apply` `a ground to end my referral exists` `the last day I attended the course or program`


§§ `Reg 77.92 -- Pilot Project No. 15, extended benefits (ended in 2012)`
-- Only if this happened to you: your benefit period was established between September 12, 2010 and the end day of the project, in a region of Schedule II.6.

@export What is the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15 in my region (reg 77.92(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the rate was under 8 percent for 12 periods in a row in my region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your region, was the regional rate of unemployment, as determined under subsection 17(1), less than 8.0% for 12 consecutive periods beginning after October 9, 2010?
      `the 12th of those periods began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the 12th of those periods begin? (Any date if the rate was not under 8.0% for 12 periods in a row.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15` IS
    `reg 77.92(2)(b) the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15` `the rate was under 8 percent for 12 periods in a row in my region` `the 12th of those periods began on`

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 15 (reg 77.92(2))?
GIVEN `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When your benefit period was established, were you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.6?
      `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `the rate was under 8 percent for 12 periods in a row in my region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your region, was the regional rate of unemployment, as determined under subsection 17(1), less than 8.0% for 12 consecutive periods beginning after October 9, 2010?
      `the 12th of those periods began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the 12th of those periods begin? (Any date if the rate was not under 8.0% for 12 periods in a row.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 15` IS
    `reg 77.92(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.6` `my benefit period was established on` (`reg 77.92(2)(b) the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15` `the rate was under 8 percent for 12 periods in a row in my region` `the 12th of those periods began on`)

@export Will the Commission publish a notice, in the Canada Gazette and on its website, of the day benefit periods stop being established in my region (reg 77.92(3))?
GIVEN `the rate was under 8 percent for 12 periods in a row in my region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your region, was the regional rate of unemployment, as determined under subsection 17(1), less than 8.0% for 12 consecutive periods beginning after October 9, 2010?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Commission publish a notice of the day benefit periods stop being established in my region` IS
    `reg 77.92(3) the Commission must publish a notice in the Canada Gazette and on its website` `the rate was under 8 percent for 12 periods in a row in my region`

@export How many weeks of benefits may I be paid in my benefit period under Pilot Project No. 15 (reg 77.92(4))?
GIVEN `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When your benefit period was established, were you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.6?
      `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `the rate was under 8 percent for 12 periods in a row in my region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In your region, was the regional rate of unemployment, as determined under subsection 17(1), less than 8.0% for 12 consecutive periods beginning after October 9, 2010?
      `the 12th of those periods began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the 12th of those periods begin? (Any date if the rate was not under 8.0% for 12 periods in a row.)
      `the weeks the table in Schedule II.7 gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks does the table in Schedule II.7 give for your regional rate of unemployment and the hours of insurable employment in your qualifying period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid under Pilot Project No. 15` IS
    `reg 77.92(4) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` (`reg 77.92(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.6` `my benefit period was established on` (`reg 77.92(2)(b) the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15` `the rate was under 8 percent for 12 periods in a row in my region` `the 12th of those periods began on`)) `the weeks the table in Schedule II.7 gives me`


§§ `Regs 77.95, 77.97 and 77.99 -- Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20, half of your earnings deducted (2012 to 2018)`
-- Only if this happened to you: you claimed benefits for a week between August 5, 2012 and August 11, 2018 and were ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I.
-- The three projects follow one another week by week (No. 18 to August 1, 2015; No. 19 from August 2, 2015 to August 6, 2016; No. 20 from August 7, 2016).

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 18, for a week I claim (reg 77.95(2))?
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the week I claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the week you claim begin?
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 18` IS
    `reg 77.95(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 18` `the Sunday that begins the week I claim` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I`

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 19, for a week I claim (reg 77.97(2))?
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the week I claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the week you claim begin?
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 19` IS
    `reg 77.97(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 19` `the Sunday that begins the week I claim` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I`

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 20, for a week I claim (reg 77.99(2))?
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the week I claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the week you claim begin?
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 20` IS
    `reg 77.99(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 20` `the Sunday that begins the week I claim` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I`

@export How much of my earnings for a week is deducted from my benefits under Pilot Project No. 18, 19 or 20 (regs 77.95(3), 77.97(3), 77.99(3), and the cessation of each section)?
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the week begin?
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I?
      `my earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you earn in the week, in dollars?
      `my weekly insurable earnings used to set my rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the weekly insurable earnings used to establish your rate of weekly benefits, in dollars?
      `the deduction is for my waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the deduction for your waiting period (the purpose of section 13 of the Act)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my earnings for a week is deducted under Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20` IS
    `reg 77.95(3), reg 77.97(3) and reg 77.99(3) the amount to be deducted for the week under whichever pilot project governs` (`reg 77.95(5), reg 77.97(5) and reg 77.99(5) one of Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20 governs the deduction for the week` `the Sunday that begins the week` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I`) `my earnings for the week` `my weekly insurable earnings used to set my rate` `the deduction is for my waiting period`

@export As a self-employed person, how much of my earnings for a week is deducted from my benefits under Pilot Project No. 18, 19 or 20 (regs 77.95(4), 77.97(4), 77.99(4))?
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the week begin?
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I?
      `my earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you earn in the week, in dollars?
      `the sum of the amounts of paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b) of the Act, in dollars?
      `the deduction is for my waiting period as a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the deduction for the purpose of section 152.15 of the Act (your waiting period)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my earnings for a week is deducted if I am self-employed under Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20` IS
    `reg 77.95(4), reg 77.97(4) and reg 77.99(4) the amount to be deducted for the week under whichever pilot project governs` (`reg 77.95(5), reg 77.97(5) and reg 77.99(5) one of Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20 governs the deduction for the week` `the Sunday that begins the week` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule I`) `my earnings for the week` `the sum of the amounts of paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` `the deduction is for my waiting period as a self-employed person`


§§ `Regs 77.96, 77.98 and 77.991 -- electing between the two methods of treating your earnings (2012 to 2018)`
-- Only if this happened to you: you had earnings treated under Pilot Project No. 17 (August 7, 2011 to August 4, 2012), or later had a benefit period in Pilot Project No. 18, 19 or 20,
-- and may choose to keep the larger allowable earnings of Pilot Project No. 17 instead of the 50% deduction.

@export May I elect to keep the allowable-earnings method of Pilot Project No. 17 instead of the 50% deduction of Pilot Project No. 18 (reg 77.96(2))?
GIVEN `I had earnings treated under subsection 77.94(3) from August 7, 2011 to August 4, 2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period from August 7, 2011 to August 4, 2012?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I elect to keep the allowable-earnings method under Pilot Project No. 18` IS
    `reg 77.96(2) the claimant may elect` `I had earnings treated under subsection 77.94(3) from August 7, 2011 to August 4, 2012`

@export By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under Pilot Project No. 18 (reg 77.96(3))?
GIVEN `I was sent a notification from August 5, 2012 to January 5, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a notification of payment or non-payment of benefits for a week of that benefit period issued to you between August 5, 2012 and January 5, 2013?
      `I was sent a notification after January 5, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was one issued to you after January 5, 2013?
      `the day my last notification was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last notification for a week of that benefit period issued to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under Pilot Project No. 18` IS
    `reg 77.96(3) the applicable deadline for informing the Commission of the election` `I was sent a notification from August 5, 2012 to January 5, 2013` `I was sent a notification after January 5, 2013` `the day my last notification was issued`

@export Is my election between the two methods treated as made in time, under Pilot Project No. 18, 19 or 20 (regs 77.96(4), 77.98(6), 77.991(6))?
GIVEN `I told the Commission of my election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell the Commission of your election?
      `the day I told the Commission` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you tell the Commission? (Any date if you did not.)
      `my deadline is known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a deadline for telling the Commission of your election?
      `my deadline for telling the Commission is` IS A DATE @desc What is that deadline? (Any date if there is none.)
      `I show good cause for the delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that there was good cause for any delay, throughout the period from the day the deadline expired to the day you told the Commission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my election treated as made in time` IS
    `reg 77.96(4), reg 77.98(6) and reg 77.991(6) the election is considered to have been made by the deadline` (IF `I told the Commission of my election` THEN JUST `the day I told the Commission` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `my deadline is known` THEN JUST `my deadline for telling the Commission is` ELSE NOTHING) `I show good cause for the delay`

@export Does my failure to elect for an earlier benefit period bind me for the next benefit period, under Pilot Project No. 18 (reg 77.96(5) to (7))?
GIVEN `I made no election for the earlier benefit period by its deadline` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make no election for the earlier benefit period by the deadline?
      `I had earnings in the earlier benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have earnings during the weeks of unemployment in the earlier benefit period?
      `I was notified only from August 5 to October 6, 2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a notification issued to you for weeks of the earlier benefit period between August 5, 2012 and October 6, 2012, and none for that benefit period after October 6, 2012?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my failure to elect for an earlier benefit period bind me for the next one under Pilot Project No. 18` IS
    `reg 77.96(5), (6) and (7) a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant for the subsequent benefit period` `I made no election for the earlier benefit period by its deadline` `I had earnings in the earlier benefit period` `I was notified only from August 5 to October 6, 2012`

@export Is the Commission's decision on my election under Pilot Project No. 18 closed to appeal under section 114 of the Act (reg 77.96(8)(a))?
GIVEN `the day of the Commission's decision` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Commission decide?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Commission's decision on my election closed to appeal under section 114` IS
    `reg 77.96(8)(a) the decision is not subject to appeal under section 114 of the Act` `the day of the Commission's decision`

@export Is the Commission's decision on my election under Pilot Project No. 18 closed to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act (reg 77.96(8)(b))?
GIVEN `the day of the Commission's decision` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Commission decide?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Commission's decision on my election under Pilot Project No. 18 closed to reconsideration under section 112` IS
    `reg 77.96(8)(b) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` `the day of the Commission's decision`

@export May I elect to keep the allowable-earnings method of Pilot Project No. 17 instead of the 50% deduction of Pilot Project No. 19 (reg 77.98(2))?
GIVEN `I had earnings treated under subsection 77.94(3) from August 7, 2011 to August 4, 2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period from August 7, 2011 to August 4, 2012?
      `I made every election I was entitled to make under section 77.96` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make every election you were entitled to make under section 77.96 (not counting one for a benefit period that began before August 2, 2015 whose last notification was issued on or after August 2, 2015)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I elect to keep the allowable-earnings method under Pilot Project No. 19` IS
    `reg 77.98(2) the claimant may elect` `I had earnings treated under subsection 77.94(3) from August 7, 2011 to August 4, 2012` `I made every election I was entitled to make under section 77.96`

@export Does my election under section 77.96 also apply to my earnings in the part of the benefit period that falls under Pilot Project No. 19 (reg 77.98(3))?
GIVEN `I made an election under section 77.96 for the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an election under section 77.96 for the benefit period?
      `the day my last notification was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last notification for a week of that benefit period issued to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my election under section 77.96 also cover my earnings under Pilot Project No. 19` IS
    `reg 77.98(3) the election under section 77.96 is deemed to apply to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period within the period` `I made an election under section 77.96 for the benefit period` `the day my last notification was issued`

@export Does my election under Pilot Project No. 19 also apply to my earnings before August 2, 2015 (reg 77.98(4))?
GIVEN `I made an election under subsection 77.98(2) for the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an election under subsection 77.98(2) for the benefit period?
      `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your benefit period begin?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my election under Pilot Project No. 19 also cover my earnings before August 2, 2015` IS
    `reg 77.98(4) the election also applies to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period before August 2, 2015` `I made an election under subsection 77.98(2) for the benefit period` `my benefit period began on`

@export By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under Pilot Project No. 19 (reg 77.98(5))?
GIVEN `the day my last notification was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last notification for a week of that benefit period issued to you?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under Pilot Project No. 19` IS
    `reg 77.98(5) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of their election` `the day my last notification was issued`

@export Does my failure to elect for an earlier benefit period bind me for the next benefit period, under Pilot Project No. 19 (reg 77.98(7), (8))?
GIVEN `I made no election for the earlier benefit period by its deadline` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make no election for the earlier benefit period by the deadline?
      `I had earnings in the earlier benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have earnings during the weeks of unemployment in the earlier benefit period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my failure to elect for an earlier benefit period bind me for the next one under Pilot Project No. 19` IS
    `reg 77.98(7) and (8) a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant for the subsequent benefit period` `I made no election for the earlier benefit period by its deadline` `I had earnings in the earlier benefit period`

@export Is the Commission's decision on a matter related to my election under Pilot Project No. 19 closed to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act (reg 77.98(9))?
GIVEN `the decision is about my election or my failure to make one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission's decision about a matter related to your election, including your failure to make one?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Commission's decision on my election under Pilot Project No. 19 closed to reconsideration` IS
    `reg 77.98(9) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` `the decision is about my election or my failure to make one`

@export Which part of my benefit period may I apply an election to, under Pilot Project No. 20 (reg 77.991(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did (or will) your benefit period end?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of days`
DECIDE `Which part of my benefit period can I apply an election to under Pilot Project No. 20` IS
    `reg 77.991(2) the portion of the benefit period to which the claimant may apply an election` (`Period of days` OF `my benefit period began on`, `my benefit period ended on`)

@export Does my election under section 77.98 also apply to my earnings in the part of the benefit period that falls under Pilot Project No. 20 (reg 77.991(3))?
GIVEN `I made an election under section 77.98 for the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an election under section 77.98 for the benefit period?
      `the day my last notification was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last notification for a week of that benefit period issued to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my election under section 77.98 also cover my earnings under Pilot Project No. 20` IS
    `reg 77.991(3) the election under section 77.98 is deemed to apply to the earnings of the portion of the benefit period within the period` `I made an election under section 77.98 for the benefit period` `the day my last notification was issued`

@export May I make an election under Pilot Project No. 20 for a benefit period that began before August 7, 2016 (reg 77.991(4))?
GIVEN `I was eligible to make an election under section 77.98 for the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you eligible to make an election under section 77.98 for the benefit period?
      `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period ended?
      `my benefit period ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end? (Any date if it has not.)
      `the day my last notification was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last notification for a week of that benefit period issued to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make an election under Pilot Project No. 20 for a benefit period that began earlier` IS
    `reg 77.991(4) the claimant may make an election under subsection 77.991(2) in respect of the benefit period` `I was eligible to make an election under section 77.98 for the benefit period` `my benefit period began on` (IF `my benefit period has ended` THEN JUST `my benefit period ended on` ELSE NOTHING) `the day my last notification was issued`

@export By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under Pilot Project No. 20 (reg 77.991(5))?
GIVEN `the day my last notification was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last notification for a week of that benefit period issued to you?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I tell the Commission of my election under Pilot Project No. 20` IS
    `reg 77.991(5) the last day on which the claimant must inform the Commission of their election` `the day my last notification was issued`

@export Is the Commission's decision on a matter related to my election under Pilot Project No. 20 closed to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act (reg 77.991(7))?
GIVEN `the decision is about my election or my failure to make one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission's decision about a matter related to your election, including your failure to make one?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Commission's decision on my election under Pilot Project No. 20 closed to reconsideration` IS
    `reg 77.991(7) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` `the decision is about my election or my failure to make one`

@export Which method treats my earnings for the benefit period, the allowable earnings of Pilot Project No. 17 or the 50% deduction, after my election (regs 77.96(2), (5), 77.98(2), (7), 77.991(2))?
GIVEN `I may elect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May you elect (see the questions on who may elect)?
      `I elected to keep the allowable-earnings method` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you elect to have subsection 77.94(3) apply instead?
      `my election was made by the deadline` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your election considered made by the deadline?
      `a failure to elect earlier binds me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period bind you?
GIVETH A `er5 Method of treating earnings under the pilot projects`
DECIDE `Which method treats my earnings for the benefit period under Pilot Projects No. 18, 19 and 20` IS
    `reg 77.96(2), (5), reg 77.98(2), (7) and reg 77.991(2) the method of treating the earnings of the benefit period` `I may elect` `I elected to keep the allowable-earnings method` `my election was made by the deadline` `a failure to elect earlier binds me`


§§ `Reg 77.992 -- Pilot Project No. 21, increased weeks for seasonal workers (ended in 2021)`
-- Only if this happened to you: your benefit period was established between August 5, 2018 and September 25, 2021, in a region of Schedule II.92, and you had earlier benefit periods in the 260 weeks before it.

@export Did an earlier benefit period of mine begin around the same time of year as my present one (reg 77.992(4))?
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the first week of my present benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the first week of your present benefit period begin?
      `the day the earlier benefit period began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the earlier benefit period begin?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did an earlier benefit period of mine begin around the same time of year` IS
    `reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` `the Sunday that begins the first week of my present benefit period` `the day the earlier benefit period began`

@export Does an earlier benefit period of mine count as established within the 260 weeks before my present one (reg 77.992(3))?
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the first week of my present benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the first week of your present benefit period begin?
      `the day the earlier benefit period was established` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the earlier benefit period established?
      `I was sent a notification for a week in the 260 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive a notification of payment or non-payment for any week that falls within those 260 weeks?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an earlier benefit period of mine count as established in the last 260 weeks` IS
    `reg 77.992(3) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260-week period` `the Sunday that begins the first week of my present benefit period` `the day the earlier benefit period was established` `I was sent a notification for a week in the 260 weeks`

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 21 (reg 77.992(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.92` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When it was established, were you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.92?
      `the earlier benefit periods with regular benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How many benefit periods were established in the 260 weeks before this one during which regular benefits were paid or payable?
      `those that began around the same time of year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those began around the same time of year as this one?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 21` IS
    `reg 77.992(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` `my benefit period was established on` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.92` (`reg 77.992(2)(c) at least three benefit periods had been established` `the earlier benefit periods with regular benefits`) (`reg 77.992(2)(d) at least two of those benefit periods had begun around the same time of year` `those that began around the same time of year`)

@export How many weeks of benefits may I be paid in my benefit period under Pilot Project No. 21 (reg 77.992(5))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.92` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When it was established, were you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I that is set out in Schedule II.92?
      `the earlier benefit periods with regular benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How many benefit periods were established in the 260 weeks before this one during which regular benefits were paid or payable?
      `those that began around the same time of year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those began around the same time of year as this one?
      `the weeks the table in Schedule II.93 gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks does the table in Schedule II.93 give for your regional rate of unemployment and the hours of insurable employment in your qualifying period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid under Pilot Project No. 21` IS
    `reg 77.992(5) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` (`reg 77.992(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` `my benefit period was established on` `I am ordinarily resident in a region of Schedule II.92` (`reg 77.992(2)(c) at least three benefit periods had been established` `the earlier benefit periods with regular benefits`) (`reg 77.992(2)(d) at least two of those benefit periods had begun around the same time of year` `those that began around the same time of year`)) `the weeks the table in Schedule II.93 gives me`


§§ `Reg 77.993 -- Pilot Project No. 22, additional weeks for seasonal workers (ended in 2024)`
-- Only if this happened to you: your benefit period was established between September 10, 2023 and September 7, 2024.

@export Am I included in Pilot Project No. 22 (reg 77.993(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your benefit period established?
      `I meet the conditions of subsection 12(2.3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the conditions set out in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act, reading Schedule II.94 of the Regulations in place of Schedule V?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I included in Pilot Project No. 22` IS
    `reg 77.993(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 22` `my benefit period was established on` `I meet the conditions of subsection 12(2.3) of the Act`

@export Which schedule is read in place of Schedule V in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act for Pilot Project No. 22 (reg 77.993(3))?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Which schedule is read in place of Schedule V for Pilot Project No. 22` IS
    `reg 77.993(3) the schedule that is read in place of Schedule V in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act`


§§ `Reg 77.994 -- Pilot Project No. 23, additional hours after natural disasters (ended in 2025)`
-- Only if this happened to you: you made an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with the postal code T0E 1E0, T0E 0C0 or R0B 1C0.
-- The text never says on which day the regulation came into force; you are asked for it.

@export How many additional hours of insurable employment am I deemed to have in my qualifying period for my claim, under Pilot Project No. 23 (reg 77.994(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `I made an initial claim for benefits under Part I of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an initial claim for benefits under Part I of the Act?
      `my postal code was` IS A STRING @desc What was the postal code of the area where you were ordinarily resident when you made the initial claim? (Write it with a space, for example T0E 1E0.)
      `a benefit period was established for my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a benefit period established for your claim?
      `my benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your benefit period begin? (Any date if none was established.)
      `my benefit period ended under paragraph 10(8)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your benefit period end in accordance with paragraph 10(8)(d) of the Act?
      `my benefit period ended under paragraph 10(8)(d) on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end that way? (Any date if it did not.)
      `I made my claim on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the claim?
      `regulation 77.994 came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 77.994 of the Regulations come into force?
      `a benefit period was established for a previous claim made after the section came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a benefit period established for you in respect of a previous claim made on or after the day the section came into force?
      `I made a previous claim with a benefit period that began before the section came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a previous claim for which a benefit period beginning before the section came into force was established?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many additional hours of insurable employment am I deemed to have under Pilot Project No. 23` IS
    `reg 77.994(2) to (4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have for the claim` `I made an initial claim for benefits under Part I of the Act` `my postal code was` `a benefit period was established for my claim` `my benefit period began on` (IF `my benefit period ended under paragraph 10(8)(d)` THEN JUST `my benefit period ended under paragraph 10(8)(d) on` ELSE NOTHING) `I made my claim on` `regulation 77.994 came into force on` `a benefit period was established for a previous claim made after the section came into force` `I made a previous claim with a benefit period that began before the section came into force`

@export Do the additional hours I am deemed to have count as hours of insurable employment for a given provision (reg 77.994(5))?
GIVEN `the hours are additional hours I am deemed to have` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they additional hours that you are deemed to have under subsection 77.994(3) or (4)?
      `the provision is` IS A STRING @desc Which provision? One of: "subsection 28(4) of the Act", "paragraph 30(1)(a) of the Act", "paragraph 31(c) of the Act", "paragraph 32(2)(c) of the Act", "subsection 35(3) of the Regulations", "subparagraph 35(7)(e)(ii) of the Regulations".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my additional hours count as hours of insurable employment for a given provision` IS
    `reg 77.994(5) the additional hours are also considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of the provision` `the hours are additional hours I am deemed to have` `the provision is`


§§ `Regs 77.996 to 77.999 -- Pilot Project No. 24, measures for major changes in economic conditions (March 30, 2025 to October 10, 2026)`
-- Only if this happened to you: your benefit period begins, or your lay-off or separation earnings fall, between March 30, 2025 and October 10, 2026.

@export May the Commission waive my waiting period (reg 77.996)?
GIVEN `my benefit period begins on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your benefit period begin?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission waive my waiting period` IS
    `reg 77.996 the Commission may waive the waiting period` `my benefit period begins on`

@export Is my waiting period waived (reg 77.996)?
GIVEN `my benefit period begins on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your benefit period begin?
      `the Commission decided to waive my waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission decided to waive your waiting period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my waiting period waived` IS
    `reg 77.996 the waiting period is waived` `my benefit period begins on` `the Commission decided to waive my waiting period`

@export Do the earnings paid to me because of a lay-off or separation stop counting as earnings for the purposes of subsection 35(2) (reg 77.997)?
GIVEN `the earnings are paid because of a lay-off or separation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the earnings paid or payable to you because of a lay-off or separation from an employment?
      `my benefit period begins on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your benefit period begin?
      `the Sunday of the first week those earnings would be allocated to` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the first week begin to which those earnings would otherwise be allocated under subsections 36(9) to (11)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my lay-off or separation earnings stop counting as earnings` IS
    `reg 77.997 earnings paid by reason of a lay-off or separation do not constitute earnings for the purposes of subsection 35(2)` `the earnings are paid because of a lay-off or separation` `my benefit period begins on` `the Sunday of the first week those earnings would be allocated to`

@export What regional rate of unemployment applies to me, as a fraction (6.5% is 0.065) (reg 77.998)?
GIVEN `the Sunday on which the later of my two weeks begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date (a Sunday) does the later of the weeks referred to in subsection 10(1) of the Act begin?
      `the rate under regulation 17` IS A NUMBER @desc What regional rate of unemployment applies to you under section 17 of the Regulations, as a fraction (6.5% is 0.065)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What regional rate of unemployment applies to me under Pilot Project No. 24` IS
    `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` `the Sunday on which the later of my two weeks begins` `the rate under regulation 17`

@export Am I a long-tenured worker (reg 77.999(1))?
GIVEN `the weeks of regular benefits I was paid in the last 156 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of regular benefits were you paid in the 156 weeks before your benefit period began?
      `my return for last year is filed and assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your income tax return for the year before your benefit period began been filed, and a notice of assessment for that year sent?
      `the years of 30 percent premiums in the last 10` IS A NUMBER @desc According to your assessed returns, in how many of the 10 years before your benefit period began did you pay at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium?
      `the years of 30 percent premiums in the 10 before last year` IS A NUMBER @desc If your return for last year is not yet filed or assessed: in how many of the 10 years before that year did you pay at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a long-tenured worker` IS
    `reg 77.999(1) long-tenured worker` `the weeks of regular benefits I was paid in the last 156 weeks` `my return for last year is filed and assessed` `the years of 30 percent premiums in the last 10` `the years of 30 percent premiums in the 10 before last year`

@export By how many weeks is my benefit period extended (reg 77.999(2))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established under section 9 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your benefit period established in accordance with section 9 of the Act?
      `my benefit period begins on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your benefit period begin?
      `my benefit period ended early under paragraph 10(8)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your benefit period end in accordance with paragraph 10(8)(d) of the Act?
      `my benefit period ended early on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it end that way? (Any date if it did not.)
      `regulation 77.999 came into force on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did section 77.999 of the Regulations come into force?
      `I am a long-tenured worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a long-tenured worker?
      `I was paid at least one week of regular or section 25 benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been paid at least one week of regular benefits, or of benefits by virtue of section 25 of the Act, in this benefit period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how many weeks is my benefit period extended under Pilot Project No. 24` IS
    `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` `my benefit period was established under section 9 of the Act` `my benefit period begins on` (IF `my benefit period ended early under paragraph 10(8)(d)` THEN JUST `my benefit period ended early on` ELSE NOTHING) `regulation 77.999 came into force on` `I am a long-tenured worker` `I was paid at least one week of regular or section 25 benefits`

@export How many weeks long can my benefit period be after all its extensions (reg 77.999(3))?
GIVEN `my benefit period begins on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your benefit period begin?
      `the length my benefit period would have with the extensions` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks long would your benefit period be after the extensions under subsections 10(10) to (13.02) of the Act and under subsection 77.999(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How long can my benefit period be after its extensions under Pilot Project No. 24` IS
    `reg 77.999(3) the length in weeks of the benefit period after its extensions, held to 104 weeks` `my benefit period begins on` `the length my benefit period would have with the extensions`

@export How many weeks of benefits for a reason other than those in subsection 12(3) of the Act can I be paid, after the extension (reg 77.999(4)(a))?
GIVEN `the maximum weeks subsection 12(2) or (2.3) gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks does subsection 12(2) or (2.3) of the Act give you as the maximum?
      `my benefit period has been extended under subsection 77.999(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period been extended under subsection 77.999(2)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of regular benefits can I be paid after the extension under Pilot Project No. 24` IS
    `reg 77.999(4)(a) the maximum number of weeks of benefits for a reason other than one mentioned in subsection 12(3) of the Act` `the maximum weeks subsection 12(2) or (2.3) gives me` `my benefit period has been extended under subsection 77.999(2)`

@export How many weeks does the reference in subsection 12(6) of the Act count for me (reg 77.999(4)(b))?
GIVEN `my benefit period has been extended under subsection 77.999(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period been extended under subsection 77.999(2)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks does subsection 12(6) of the Act count for me under Pilot Project No. 24` IS
    `reg 77.999(4)(b) the number of weeks that subsection 12(6) of the Act refers to` `my benefit period has been extended under subsection 77.999(2)`

@export Do my additional weeks of benefits stay payable if I stop being a long-tenured worker during my benefit period (reg 77.999(5))?
GIVEN `my benefit period has been extended under subsection 77.999(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period been extended under subsection 77.999(2)?
      `I stopped being a long-tenured worker during my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stop being a long-tenured worker during your benefit period?
      `another reason ends my right to the additional weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does some other reason end your right to the additional weeks?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my additional weeks stay payable if I stop being a long-tenured worker` IS
    `reg 77.999(5) the additional weeks are still payable` `my benefit period has been extended under subsection 77.999(2)` `I stopped being a long-tenured worker during my benefit period` `another reason ends my right to the additional weeks`


§§ `Regs 78 and 79 -- asking the Commission to reconsider a decision`
-- Only if this happened to you: the Commission made a decision about your claim and you want it reconsidered under section 112 of the Act.

@export Is my request for reconsideration in writing and does it contain the information the regulation requires (reg 78(1))?
GIVEN `my request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing?
      `my request gives my name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give your name?
      `my request gives my social insurance number or business number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give your social insurance number, or the business number assigned to you by the Minister of National Revenue?
      `my request gives my address and telephone number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give your address and telephone number?
      `I have a facsimile number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a facsimile (fax) number?
      `my request gives my facsimile number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give your fax number? (No if you have none.)
      `I have an email address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an email address?
      `my request gives my email address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give your email address? (No if you have none.)
      `my request gives the day the decision was communicated to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the date on which the decision was communicated to you?
      `my request gives my reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give your reasons for asking for reconsideration?
      `I have relevant information I did not give the Commission before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have any relevant information that you did not previously give the Commission?
      `my request contains that information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request contain that information? (Yes if you have none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my request for reconsideration contain what regulation 78 requires` IS
    `reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` `my request is in writing` `my request gives my name` `my request gives my social insurance number or business number` `my request gives my address and telephone number` `I have a facsimile number` `my request gives my facsimile number` `I have an email address` `my request gives my email address` `my request gives the day the decision was communicated to me` `my request gives my reasons` `I have relevant information I did not give the Commission before` `my request contains that information`

@export Did I file my request for reconsideration at the address, fax number or email address, or by the electronic filing procedure, that the Commission's website provides (reg 78(2))?
GIVEN `I filed at the address on the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file it at the address the Commission provides on the website of the Department of Employment and Social Development?
      `I filed at the fax number on the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file it at the fax number the Commission provides on that website?
      `I filed at the email address on the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file it at the email address the Commission provides on that website?
      `I filed by the electronic filing procedure on the website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file it by the electronic filing procedure the Commission provides on that website?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I file my request for reconsideration the way the Commission's website provides` IS
    `reg 78(2) the request for reconsideration was filed as the Commission's website provides` `I filed at the address on the website` `I filed at the fax number on the website` `I filed at the email address on the website` `I filed by the electronic filing procedure on the website`

@export Must the Commission decide my request for reconsideration without delay (reg 79)?
GIVEN `I have made a request for reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a request for reconsideration of a decision of the Commission?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commission decide my request for reconsideration without delay` IS
    `reg 79 the Commission must render its decision on the request without delay` `I have made a request for reconsideration`

-- The regulation gives no number of days for 'without delay': the answer is NOTHING, which is not 'yes' and not 'no'.
@export Has the Commission taken too long to decide my request for reconsideration (reg 79)?
GIVEN `the days since I made my request` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since you made your request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Commission taken too long to decide my request for reconsideration` IS
    `reg 79 the Commission has rendered its decision without delay` `the days since I made my request`


§§ `Regs 80 to 82 -- benefits held back while the Commission appeals`
-- Only if this happened to you: the Social Security Tribunal (or the Board of Appeal) decided in your favour and the Commission appealed or applied for judicial review.

@export Are my benefits not payable under the tribunal's decision because the Commission appealed it to the Appeal Division within 21 days (reg 80)?
GIVEN `the day the decision was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the decision of the Employment Insurance Section (or the Board of Appeal) given?
      `the Commission appealed to the Appeal Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission appeal that decision to the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal?
      `the day the Commission appealed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it appeal? (Any date if it did not.)
      `the Commission's ground is an error in law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission's ground that the Employment Insurance Section or the Board of Appeal erred in law?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my benefits held back because the Commission appealed the tribunal's decision` IS
    `reg 80 benefits are not payable in accordance with the decision` `the day the decision was given` (IF `the Commission appealed to the Appeal Division` THEN JUST `the day the Commission appealed` ELSE NOTHING) `the Commission's ground is an error in law`

@export Are my benefits not payable on my claim because the Commission applied for judicial review of the Appeal Division's decision (reg 81)?
GIVEN `my claim is the one the Appeal Division decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim the one that is the object of the Appeal Division's decision?
      `the Commission applied for judicial review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission apply under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of that decision?
      `that application has been finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that application been finally determined?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my benefits held back because the Commission applied for judicial review` IS
    `reg 81 benefits are not payable in respect of the claim` `my claim is the one the Appeal Division decided` `the Commission applied for judicial review` `that application has been finally determined`

@export Is my claim caught by a decision that declares a provision of the Act or the Regulations ultra vires (reg 82(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my claim is the one the decision is about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim the one that is the object of the decision?
      `I made my claim after the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your claim after that decision?
      `I would be paid but for the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would benefits be payable on your claim except for that decision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim caught by a decision that a provision is ultra vires` IS
    `reg 82(1) and (2) the claim is caught by the decision` `my claim is the one the decision is about` `I made my claim after the decision` `I would be paid but for the decision`

@export Are my benefits not payable because the Commission appealed a decision that declares a provision ultra vires (reg 82(1))?
GIVEN `the decision is a General Division decision that a provision of the Act or Regulations is ultra vires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one of the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal declaring a provision of the Act or the Regulations ultra vires?
      `the decision is a Board of Appeal decision that a provision of the Regulations is ultra vires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it instead a decision of the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal declaring a provision of the Regulations ultra vires?
      `the Commission appealed to the Appeal Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission appeal the decision to the Appeal Division?
      `my claim is caught by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim caught by the decision (the claim it is about, or a later claim that would be payable but for it)?
      `the Appeal Division finally determined the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Appeal Division made its final determination of the appeal?
      `that determination declares the provision ultra vires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that final determination declare the provision ultra vires?
      `the Commission applied for judicial review of that determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission apply under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of that determination?
      `that application has been finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that application been finally determined?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my benefits held back because the Commission appealed a decision that a provision is ultra vires` IS
    `reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` `the decision is a General Division decision that a provision of the Act or Regulations is ultra vires` `the decision is a Board of Appeal decision that a provision of the Regulations is ultra vires` `the Commission appealed to the Appeal Division` `my claim is caught by the decision` `the Appeal Division finally determined the appeal` `that determination declares the provision ultra vires` `the Commission applied for judicial review of that determination` `that application has been finally determined`

@export Are my benefits not payable because the Commission applied for judicial review of an Appeal Division decision that declares a provision ultra vires (reg 82(2))?
GIVEN `the Appeal Division's decision declares a provision ultra vires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Appeal Division's decision declare a provision of the Act or the Regulations ultra vires?
      `the Commission applied for judicial review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission apply under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of that decision?
      `my claim is caught by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim caught by the decision (the claim it is about, or a later claim that would be payable but for it)?
      `that application has been finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that application been finally determined?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my benefits held back because the Commission applied for judicial review of a decision that a provision is ultra vires` IS
    `reg 82(2) benefits are not payable on the claim` `the Appeal Division's decision declares a provision ultra vires` `the Commission applied for judicial review` `my claim is caught by the decision` `that application has been finally determined`


§§ `Reg 88 -- benefits held back while a ruling on my insurable hours is pending`
-- Only if this happened to you: a request was made to an officer of the (former) Canada Customs and Revenue Agency for a ruling on whether you were employed in insurable employment for some hours.

@export On what day do the rulings on whether my hours are insurable become final, the officer's ruling and every appeal that was taken (reg 88(1)(a), (b))?
GIVEN `the officer's ruling is final` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the officer's ruling on the question become final?
      `the day the officer's ruling became final` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it become final? (Any date if it has not.)
      `I appealed to the Minister of National Revenue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an appeal from the ruling go to the Minister of National Revenue?
      `the Minister's decision is final` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister's decision become final?
      `the day the Minister's decision became final` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (Any date if it has not.)
      `I appealed to the Tax Court of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an appeal filed with the Tax Court of Canada under section 103 of the Act?
      `the Tax Court's decision is final` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Tax Court's decision become final?
      `the day the Tax Court's decision became final` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (Any date if it has not.)
      `I applied to the Federal Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an application made to the Federal Court of Appeal under section 28 of the Federal Courts Act to review the Tax Court's decision?
      `the Federal Court of Appeal's decision is final` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Federal Court of Appeal's decision become final?
      `the day the Federal Court of Appeal's decision became final` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (Any date if it has not.)
      `I applied to the Supreme Court of Canada for leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an application made to the Supreme Court of Canada for leave to appeal from the Federal Court of Appeal's decision?
      `the Supreme Court's final decision was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the final decision of the Supreme Court of Canada been given?
      `the day the Supreme Court's final decision was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (Any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day do the rulings on my insurable hours become final` IS
    `reg 88(1) the later of the day the officer's ruling becomes final and the day the decision at the last stage taken becomes final` (IF `the officer's ruling is final` THEN JUST `the day the officer's ruling became final` ELSE NOTHING) minister taxCourt appeal supreme
    WHERE
        `minister` MEANS
            `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling` OF `I appealed to the Minister of National Revenue`, (IF `the Minister's decision is final` THEN JUST `the day the Minister's decision became final` ELSE NOTHING)
        `taxCourt` MEANS
            `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling` OF `I appealed to the Tax Court of Canada`, (IF `the Tax Court's decision is final` THEN JUST `the day the Tax Court's decision became final` ELSE NOTHING)
        `appeal` MEANS
            `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling` OF `I applied to the Federal Court of Appeal`, (IF `the Federal Court of Appeal's decision is final` THEN JUST `the day the Federal Court of Appeal's decision became final` ELSE NOTHING)
        `supreme` MEANS
            `er5 Stage of a dispute over a ruling` OF `I applied to the Supreme Court of Canada for leave`, (IF `the Supreme Court's final decision was given` THEN JUST `the day the Supreme Court's final decision was given` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Are no benefits payable for an hour that is the subject of the ruling on a given day (reg 88(1), (2))?
GIVEN `a request for a ruling was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a request made to an officer of the Canada Customs and Revenue Agency under paragraph 90(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d) of the Act for a ruling on whether you were employed in insurable employment for some hours?
      `the hour is one of the hours under ruling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hour you ask about one of the hours that is the subject of the ruling?
      `I qualify on other hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits on the basis of hours of insurable employment other than the hours that are the subject of the application?
      `the rulings are all final` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the officer's ruling and every appeal that was taken become final?
      `the day the last ruling became final` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the last of them become final? (Any date if they have not all become final.)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask whether benefits are payable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are benefits not payable for the hours under ruling on a given day` IS
    `reg 88(1) no benefits are payable in respect of the hour on the day in question` `a request for a ruling was made` `the hour is one of the hours under ruling` `I qualify on other hours` (IF `the rulings are all final` THEN JUST `the day the last ruling became final` ELSE NOTHING) `the day I ask about`


§§ `Reg 89 -- my Social Insurance Number`
-- Only if you start a job that is insurable employment.

@export Must I apply to the Commission to be registered for a Social Insurance Number (reg 89(1))?
GIVEN `my employment is insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment insurable employment?
      `section 138 of the Act requires me to have a Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 138 of the Act require you to have a Social Insurance Number?
      `I have not yet applied to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not yet applied to the Commission to be registered?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I apply to the Commission to be registered for a Social Insurance Number` IS
    `reg 89(1) the person must apply to the Commission to be registered` `my employment is insurable employment` `section 138 of the Act requires me to have a Social Insurance Number` `I have not yet applied to be registered`

@export By what day must I apply to the Commission to be registered (reg 89(1))?
GIVEN `the day my employment begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your employment begin?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I apply to be registered for a Social Insurance Number` IS
    `reg 89(1) the last day on which the person must apply to be registered` `the day my employment begins`

@export Did I apply to be registered within three days after my employment began (reg 89(1))?
GIVEN `the day my employment begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your employment begin?
      `the day I applied to be registered` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply to be registered?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I apply to be registered in time` IS
    `reg 89(1) the person applies to be registered within three days after the day on which the employment begins` `the day my employment begins` `the day I applied to be registered`

-- An employer's duty, asked as what is done to the employee: when my employer must ask me. NOTHING when no employer is bound to ask.
@export By what day must my employer ask me to tell it my Social Insurance Number (reg 89(2))?
GIVEN `my employer hired me in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer hire you in insurable employment?
      `the day my employment begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your employment begin?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my employer ask me for my Social Insurance Number` IS
    IF `reg 89(2) the employer must ask the employee to inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` `my employer hired me in insurable employment` THEN JUST (`reg 89(2) the last day on which the employer must ask the employee` `the day my employment begins`) ELSE NOTHING

@export By what day must I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number (reg 89(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the day my employment begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your employment begin?
      `I became employed before I was registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become employed before you were registered for a Social Insurance Number?
      `I have received my number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received your Social Insurance Number?
      `the day I received my number` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive it? (Any date if you have not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number` IS
    `reg 89(3) and (4) the last day on which the person must inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` `the day my employment begins` `I became employed before I was registered` (IF `I have received my number` THEN JUST `the day I received my number` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Did I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number in time (reg 89(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the day my employment begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your employment begin?
      `I became employed before I was registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become employed before you were registered for a Social Insurance Number?
      `I have received my number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received your Social Insurance Number?
      `the day I received my number` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive it? (Any date if you have not.)
      `I have told my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told your employer your number?
      `the day I told my employer` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you tell your employer? (Any date if you have not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I tell my employer my Social Insurance Number in time` IS
    `reg 89(3) and (4) the person informs the employer of their Social Insurance Number in time` (`reg 89(3) and (4) the last day on which the person must inform the employer of their Social Insurance Number` `the day my employment begins` `I became employed before I was registered` (IF `I have received my number` THEN JUST `the day I received my number` ELSE NOTHING)) (IF `I have told my employer` THEN JUST `the day I told my employer` ELSE NOTHING)

-- An employer's duty, asked as what is done on my account: when my employer must report. NOTHING when no duty has arisen.
@export By what day must my employer report to the Commission if it cannot ascertain my Social Insurance Number (reg 89(5))?
GIVEN `my employer is unable to ascertain my Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer unable to ascertain your Social Insurance Number?
      `the day my employment begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your employment begin?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my employer report to the Commission if it cannot ascertain my Social Insurance Number` IS
    IF `reg 89(5) the employer must report the matter to the local office of the Commission` `my employer is unable to ascertain my Social Insurance Number` THEN JUST (`reg 89(5) the last day on which the employer must report the matter` `the day my employment begins`) ELSE NOTHING

@export Must I tell my employer that my Social Insurance Number, or its period of validity, has changed (reg 89(6))?
GIVEN `I am employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in insurable employment?
      `the validity of my number was extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the period of validity of your Social Insurance Number been extended?
      `a new period of validity was assigned to my number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a new period of validity been assigned to your number?
      `a new number was assigned to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a new Social Insurance Number been assigned to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell my employer that my Social Insurance Number or its validity has changed` IS
    `reg 89(6) the person must inform their employer of the change` `I am employed in insurable employment` `the validity of my number was extended` `a new period of validity was assigned to my number` `a new number was assigned to me`

@export By what day must I tell my employer of the change (reg 89(6))?
GIVEN `the day I was told of the change` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you informed of the change?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I tell my employer of the change in my Social Insurance Number` IS
    `reg 89(6) the last day on which the person must inform their employer of the change` `the day I was told of the change`

@export Did I tell my employer of the change within three days after I was informed of it (reg 89(6))?
GIVEN `the day I was told of the change` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you informed of the change?
      `the day I told my employer of the change` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you tell your employer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I tell my employer of the change in time` IS
    `reg 89(6) the person informs their employer of the change within three days after the day they are informed of it` `the day I was told of the change` `the day I told my employer of the change`


§§ `Regs 90 and 91 -- giving the Commission information and claiming by telephone or online`
-- Only if you gave the Commission information, or made a claim, by telephone or other electronic means.

@export Must the information I give the Commission be in a form and manner the Commission approves (reg 90)?
GIVEN `I am providing information to the Commission for the purposes of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you providing information to the Commission, in electronic or other form, for the purposes of the Act or its regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must information I give the Commission be in a form and manner it approves` IS
    `reg 90 the information must be provided in a form and manner approved by the Commission` `I am providing information to the Commission for the purposes of the Act`

@export Is the information I gave provided in the way the Commission requires (reg 90)?
GIVEN `I am providing information to the Commission for the purposes of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you providing information to the Commission, in electronic or other form, for the purposes of the Act or its regulations?
      `the Commission approved the form and manner I used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form and manner you used one the Commission has approved?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the information I gave provided as the Commission requires` IS
    `reg 90 the information is provided as the Commission requires` `I am providing information to the Commission for the purposes of the Act` `the Commission approved the form and manner I used`

@export Am I treated as having made my claim when I made it by telephone or other electronic means (reg 91(1)(a))?
GIVEN `I claimed by telephone or other electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your initial claim, or your claim for a week of unemployment, by telephone or other electronic means?
      `I gave the information section 50 of the Act requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the information that section 50 of the Act requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having made my claim when I claimed by telephone or online` IS
    `reg 91(1)(a) the claimant is deemed to have expressed an intention to make a claim and to have made it for the purposes of section 48, 49 or 152.1 of the Act` (`reg 91(1) the claim is made by telephone or other electronic means with the information section 50 requires` `I claimed by telephone or other electronic means` `I gave the information section 50 of the Act requires`)

@export Am I treated as having supplied the information recorded on the Commission's dated printout as my answers to its questions (reg 91(1)(b))?
GIVEN `I claimed by telephone or other electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your initial claim, or your claim for a week of unemployment, by telephone or other electronic means?
      `I gave the information section 50 of the Act requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the information that section 50 of the Act requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having answered the questions when I claimed by telephone or online` IS
    `reg 91(1)(b) the claimant is deemed to have supplied the information on the dated printout as responses to the questions of the interactive response system` (`reg 91(1) the claim is made by telephone or other electronic means with the information section 50 requires` `I claimed by telephone or other electronic means` `I gave the information section 50 of the Act requires`)

@export Am I treated as having signed my claim when I made it by telephone or other electronic means (reg 91(2))?
GIVEN `the kind of claim I made` IS A `er5 Kind of claim made by telephone or other electronic means` @desc Which kind of claim was it: `er5 an initial claim for benefits` or `er5 a claim for benefits for a week of unemployment`?
      `I gave my Social Insurance Number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your Social Insurance Number by telephone or other electronic means?
      `I gave my date of birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your date of birth? (For an initial claim.)
      `my initial claim was by electronic means other than telephone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your initial claim made by electronic means other than telephone?
      `I gave my mother's maiden name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your mother's maiden name? (For an initial claim made by electronic means other than telephone.)
      `I gave my personal identification number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give your personal identification number? (For a claim for a week of unemployment.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having signed my claim when I claimed by telephone or online` IS
    `reg 91(2) the claimant is deemed to have signed the claim` `the kind of claim I made` `I gave my Social Insurance Number` `I gave my date of birth` `my initial claim was by electronic means other than telephone` `I gave my mother's maiden name` `I gave my personal identification number`

@export On what day is my claim, made by telephone or other electronic means, treated as made (reg 91(3))?
GIVEN `I claimed by the means referred to in subsection 91(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the claim by telephone or other electronic means, as subsection 91(1) describes?
      `the day the Commission's system received and recorded the information` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Commission's computerized benefit pay system receive and record the information?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my claim by telephone or online treated as made` IS
    `reg 91(3) the day on which the claim is deemed to have been made` `I claimed by the means referred to in subsection 91(1)` `the day the Commission's system received and recorded the information`

@export Do sections 38 and 135 of the Act (false statements; penalty and punishment) apply to a declaration I make by electronic means (reg 91(4))?
GIVEN `my declaration is made by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your declaration made by electronic means?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the false-statement provisions apply to a declaration I make electronically` IS
    `reg 91(4) sections 38 and 135 of the Act apply to the declaration` `my declaration is made by electronic means`

@export Can I be refused access to the electronic systems used in administering the Act if I knowingly try to interfere with their operation (reg 91(5))?
GIVEN `I knowingly attempt to interfere with the electronic systems` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you knowingly attempt to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used in the administration of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be refused access to the Commission's electronic systems if I try to interfere with them` IS
    `reg 91(5) the penalty and the punishment include the right to refuse the person access to the electronic systems` `I knowingly attempt to interfere with the electronic systems`

@export Does knowingly attempting to interfere with the electronic systems count as an act or omission of sections 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act (reg 91(5))?
GIVEN `I knowingly attempt to interfere with the electronic systems` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you knowingly attempt to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used in the administration of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my attempt to interfere with the electronic systems count as an offence of section 38 or 135` IS
    `reg 91(5) the act is deemed to be an act or omission specified in subsections 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act` `I knowingly attempt to interfere with the electronic systems`


§§ `Reg 92 -- direct deposit of my benefits`
-- Only if you gave the Commission a bank account number for the direct deposit of your benefits.

@export Which sections of the Direct Deposit Regulations apply to my direct deposit (reg 92(1))?
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `Which sections of the Direct Deposit Regulations apply to me` IS
    `reg 92(1) the sections of the Direct Deposit Regulations that apply for the purposes of this section`

@export Will my benefits be deposited directly to my bank account (reg 92(2))?
GIVEN `I gave the Commission an account number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the Commission the number of a bank account?
      `the account is active` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the account active?
      `the account is registered in my name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the account registered in your name?
      `the account is in a financial institution in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in a financial institution in Canada?
      `I was refused access to the direct deposit systems` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been refused access to the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits, under subsection 92(7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my benefits be deposited directly to my bank account` IS
    `reg 92(2) the claimant's benefits are to be deposited directly to their bank account` `I gave the Commission an account number` `the account is active` `the account is registered in my name` `the account is in a financial institution in Canada` `I was refused access to the direct deposit systems`

@export Am I responsible for the accuracy of the data I gave to register for direct deposit (reg 92(3))?
GIVEN `I supplied the data in order to register for direct deposit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you supply the data in order to register for the direct deposit of benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I responsible for the accuracy of the bank details I gave` IS
    `reg 92(3) the claimant is responsible for the accuracy of the data` `I supplied the data in order to register for direct deposit`

-- NOTHING when there is contrary evidence or a document is missing: the regulation says what the documents are worth only when both exist and nothing contradicts them.
@export Do the Commission's certified extract and my financial institution's certified extract together count as evidence that my benefits were deposited and paid (reg 92(4))?
GIVEN `there is no evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there no evidence to the contrary?
      `there is a certified extract from the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a document certified by a person acting for the Commission to be an extract from the record authorizing a direct deposit transaction to the financial institution where your account is?
      `there is a certified extract from my financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a certified extract of your financial institution's records showing the deposit credited to your account?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the Commission's documents prove my benefits were deposited` IS
    `reg 92(4) the documents together constitute evidence of the transfer of funds and the payment of benefits` `there is no evidence to the contrary` `there is a certified extract from the Commission` `there is a certified extract from my financial institution`

@export Must I notify the Commission to end the direct deposit of my benefits (reg 92(5))?
GIVEN `I wish to end my direct deposit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to terminate the direct deposit of your benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I notify the Commission to stop my direct deposit` IS
    `reg 92(5) the claimant must notify the Commission` `I wish to end my direct deposit`

@export Has my direct deposit of benefits ended (reg 92(5))?
GIVEN `I wish to end my direct deposit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to terminate the direct deposit of your benefits?
      `I have notified the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the Commission?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my direct deposit ended` IS
    `reg 92(5) the direct deposit of benefits is terminated` `I wish to end my direct deposit` `I have notified the Commission`

@export Do sections 38 and 135 of the Act apply to a declaration I make about the payment of my benefits (reg 92(6))?
GIVEN `my declaration is made in the context of the payment of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your declaration made in the context of the payment of benefits under regulation 92?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the false-statement provisions apply to a declaration I make about my payment` IS
    `reg 92(6) sections 38 and 135 of the Act apply to the declaration` `my declaration is made in the context of the payment of benefits`

@export Can I be refused access to the electronic systems used for direct deposit if I knowingly try to interfere with their operation (reg 92(7))?
GIVEN `I knowingly attempt to interfere with the direct deposit systems` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you knowingly attempt to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be refused access to the direct deposit systems if I try to interfere with them` IS
    `reg 92(7) the penalty and the punishment include the right to refuse the person access to the electronic systems used for direct deposit` `I knowingly attempt to interfere with the direct deposit systems`

@export Does knowingly attempting to interfere with the direct deposit systems count as an act or omission of sections 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act (reg 92(7))?
GIVEN `I knowingly attempt to interfere with the direct deposit systems` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you knowingly attempt to interfere with the operation of the electronic systems used for the direct deposit of benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my attempt to interfere with the direct deposit systems count as an offence of section 38 or 135` IS
    `reg 92(7) the act is deemed to be an act or omission specified in subsections 38(1) and 135(1) of the Act` `I knowingly attempt to interfere with the direct deposit systems`

@export May the Commission redirect my direct deposit when my financial institution tells it of a change (reg 92(8))?
GIVEN `I have told the Commission otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you advised the Commission that it is not to redirect your deposit?
      `my benefits go to an active account whose number I gave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your benefits deposited to an active account at a financial institution, the number of which you gave the Commission?
      `my financial institution told the Commission of a change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the financial institution notified the Commission of a change of the financial institution, branch or account number?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission redirect my direct deposit to another account` IS
    `reg 92(8) the Commission may redirect the deposit of benefits` `I have told the Commission otherwise` `my benefits go to an active account whose number I gave` `my financial institution told the Commission of a change`
